ange as well, but that will be handled by the larger ```"]],0,426],[7123104,20399,8,0.807,0.615,[[13,22]],[["d3e138e8_2a6a7183",62,-2,1,"```suggestion name=\"LOCAL_NETWORK_ACCESS\">Local Network Access</ph> checks failing, the ```"],["ed317b61_9d7855ac",62,-2,1,"```suggestion Network Access</ph> has launched by default. The policy will be removed in a ```"],["e1c030ff_fd15dbc2",62,-1,0,"Do you know which milestone should be the last? If not, please add a todo to add it."]],0,427],[7132119,20399,7,0.552,0.402,[[13,23]],[],0,428],[7142519,20403,8,0.317,0.238,[[0,34]],[],0,429],[7116538,20405,524,14.16,11.893,[[2,0.668,24,358],[0,0.277,35,138],[26,0.026,52,12],[41,0.009,8,4],[4,0.009,24,4],[10,0.007,5,3],[71,0.004,1,1]],[["1a13be97_015802d8",58,-8,1,"```suggestion // Error here is that we initially saw the response in the ```"],["28ed950b_f3228201",5,-8,1,"to"],["2eb09c9e_d567b29e",5,-8,1,"\"This is set if\" implies this is an optional, but it is not. Should it be an optional?"],["698d2b1e_f3d545b1",5,-8,1,"Remove extra blank line."],["835f965b_b39df5c5",5,-8,1,"nit: Here, and on the next two lines, use backticks around field names (`)"]],0,430],[7142023,20411,338,7.602,6.22,[[41,0.543,9,187],[39,0.151,40,52],[48,0.137,5,46],[7,0.094,9,32],[1,0.074,32,25]],[],0,431],[7170043,20416,153,4.57,3.75,[[0,0.582,36,89],[4,0.247,25,38],[1,0.171,33,26]],[["b5ceba72_55b1540e",63,-6,1,"IP address space"],["e6325931_65e49d22",64,-6,1,"Should we also include \" || ip_address_space == kLoopback\" here (per the \"it can't hurt\" comment above)? (And similarly in the subresource mixed_content_checker below)"],["01f3965e_64949dc2",63,-3,0,"This code also treats \"local\" as a local domain (which I assume is accurate)."],["02bd230d_376d5ace",63,-3,1,"+. at end of sentence"],["0a86ae62_24c76dc1",65,-3,0,"Optional: Yoda ordering is not discouraged by the Chromium style guide (\"Prefer `(foo == 0)` to `(0 == foo)`).\" Of course, current style is more consistent with existing code. Up to you."],["11f62cd7_11c4116e",63,-3,1,"Worth mentioning \"localhost.\" and \"local.\"?"],["4b5d9b0c_9bda3668",66,-3,0,"It is unfortunate this differs from net::IsLocalHostname(). Looks like the only difference between the two is IsLocalHostname() doesn't include :: or 0.0.0.0, but it looks to be the same otherwise,…"],["74823f49_dbb269ef",65,-3,1,"Also may want a couple more https tests, though not exactly losing sleep if we don't add any."],["d7c7935b_48bf6673",65,-3,1,"Suggest also testing `localhost.`, `foo.localhost`, `local`, and `local.` (Could check `foo.localhost.`, but think the others are sufficient)."],["f39ef1a2_670518f4",64,-3,1,"I defer to Nate on the behavior changes here and in third_party/blink/renderer/core/loader/mixed_content_checker.cc (Just to be explicit about it)"]],0,432],[7167750,20418,656,14.16,11.893,[[2,0.608,25,402],[43,0.315,12,208],[72,0.034,0,22],[26,0.024,53,15],[0,0.01,37,6],[36,0.004,54,2],[31,0.003,15,1]],[["7746a33a_4e36b6ff",67,-6,1,"Do we want a parallel test with a .local domain that _does_ resolve, but doesn't connect?"],["cf09e6f4_22ab4d59",68,-6,1,"Add a comment here about why it's okay for us to ignore the result (i.e., we will trigger the LNA permission check again later in OnConnected() and that is where we actually use the result)."],["0a675ba7_3196127c",67,-5,1,"I think this comment (and future copies of it) are confusing, since while true, it's not the fetch failing the test really cares about, but the LNA dialog not being shown, so whether we accept or…"],["119e29a2_bcf0ae76",29,-5,1,"Please move this to match declaration order (Not moving it did make the review easier, though!)"],["3bf006eb_35248f01",43,-5,1,"I think we both need a comment on what this does, and rename it to be a bit clearer, since this is more about mapping hostnames than how they're resolved (though admittedly, the map is stored in the…"],["3e338712_b610a73e",67,-5,1,"optional: Could add a helper for this, or even put it in SetUpOnMainThread"],["6bcb3b38_abc29886",68,-5,1,"I think we might want to say something about this in OnLocalNetworkAccessPermissionRequired() - it's not mentioned that it might show the prompt, or that the result might be cached by the browser…"],["7e51a6ef_a3f041a1",43,-5,1,"const? Also suggest putting this first, due to its const-ness."],["7e631689_a088df07",68,-5,0,"Is there an advantage to doing this rather than calling through the PrivateNetworkAccessUrlLoaderInterceptor's access checker? I guess this lets us bypass the checks entirely if there's no…"],["9b4b4fb9_09935848",68,-5,1,"This CL breaks the \"Security.PrivateNetworkAccess.PrivateIpInferrable\" histogram - old and new values aren't comparable, and we check an extra time for certain types of URLs when they're directly…"],["9bb40c25_7496012f",67,-5,1,"I'm not comfortable relying on \"unlikely\" here, as we don't control the environment the test is running on. We could create a net::TcpSocket, bind it to 127.0.0.1, port 0, and use whatever ephemeral…"],["abf64506_c605c8f9",67,-5,1,"We should use .test hostnames where possible, to avoid accidentally depending on real hostnames resolving. I also suggest making the hostnames constants (constexpr chars at the stop of the file, or…"],["acfd8262_1c5a15e8",67,-5,1,"optional: Could also add a helper for this that takes a GURL and fetches it."],["b6b84489_40765ebc",38,-5,1,"Remove second the and add backticks around resource_address_space."],["edefcd33_d0b992d5",67,-5,1,"nit: std::string_view, for both args (Really doesn't matter for tests, admittedly, just good to match what we'd do in production code)"],["fff53c10_c57e6bed",38,-5,1,"Suggest \"assumes that\" -> \"[in|for] the case where\""],["437e89e8_7f4e3be8",67,-1,1,"Instead of using a unique_ptr, can inline the constructor call with the variable declaration. It's recommended that unique_ptr only be used in classes when it's needed, now-a-days."],["549a4b2c_20f3ad6d",67,-1,1,"Can use the static method `net::IPAddress::IPv4Localhost();` to get this instead."],["ddb1cd1e_dbd60a17",67,-1,1,"Maybe remove deterministic here? The port varies from run-to-run. Alternatively \"this lets us have a port that will deterministically not accept any connections\""]],0,433],[7212679,20423,2100,9.499,7.568,[[39,0.617,41,1298],[43,0.381,13,800],[31,0.001,16,2]],[],0,434],[7223710,20425,11,0.421,0.3,[[43,14]],[],0,435],[7209846,20426,56,1.49,1.096,[[48,0.548,6,31],[1,0.258,34,15],[73,0.194,0,10]],[],0,436],[7002513,20426,71,2.361,1.866,[[43,0.329,15,25],[58,0.215,14,16],[13,0.203,24,14],[18,0.076,40,5],[44,0.076,24,5],[47,0.051,16,3],[59,0.051,6,3]],[["5f499cea_e95811d7",69,0,1,"Instead of deleting this file annotate it as a removed policy see components/policy/test/data/pref_mapping/NativePrinters.json for example."],["f143b708_3a99a14c",0,0,1,"Please verify that this satisfies https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/refs/heads/main/chrome/browser/prefs/README.md#deleting-an-old-pref-exposed-by-a-policy and, if so, document that it…"]],0,437],[7225793,20434,470,6.547,5.298,[[38,0.311,2,155],[43,0.153,16,77],[74,0.074,1,35],[16,0.072,6,34],[4,0.068,26,32],[75,0.063,2,29],[28,0.039,4,19],[26,0.031,54,12],[76,0.025,0,10],[5,0.025,4,12],[0,0.02,38,8],[23,0.018,60,7],[77,0.018,0,8],[8,0.018,6,8],[11,0.018,18,6],[33,0.012,1,5],[29,0.01,2,4],[78,0.01,0,4],[79,0.006,0,2],[51,0.006,1,2],[31,0.004,17,1]],[["fef23a53_626fcdbb",70,-3,0,"Squinting at this one I'm wondering why these numbers don't match the PermissionType entries in enums.xml _nor_ the RequestTypeForUma enum in…"],["27f425df_d0541114",71,-2,0,"Have you tested this? I'm pretty sure exceptions don't just mean the ones created manually via site settings, but every value that is different, which would include exceptions created by granting on…"],["de051939_6032a112",72,-1,1,"I find the naming a little weird. I guess local-network-access is going to be replaced by these two new permissions. Should we indicate (old) and (new) and then just call the new ones